=== p2-windows · W7 · page:admin/FeatureFlags (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:admin/FeatureFlags   kind=page   web route=/admin/flags
Web source  : web/src/features/admin/pages/FeatureFlagsPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked. WindowsAppSDK / maui-windows
              workload builds the full solution (verified BUILD_EXIT=0). WinAppDriver UI-automation runner (W9 scope)
              is absent, so the W7 test gate runs the headless TeslaSync.App.Tests project (the sibling-W7 convention).

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  DLQInspectorPage / FeedbackQueuePage / ApiLogsPage do. The generated prompt's idealized "FeatureFlagsPage.xaml +
  FeatureFlagsPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Admin" is mapped onto these real conventions; the surface
  registers with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("FeatureFlagsAdmin", already in RouteTable.cs → /admin/flags).
- The page COMPOSES the three feature-flag sub-surfaces that already exist (W3): FlagsTable, ChangesPanel
  (feature-views/, namespace TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.FeatureFlags) and the FlagEditDrawer create/edit side sheet
  (modals-dialogs/, namespace TeslaSync.App.ModalsDialogs). The page owns the orchestration the web page owns: the
  "Add flag" CTA + a row's Edit open the FlagEditDrawer (create vs. seeded edit); the drawer's SaveRequested routes to
  the set-flag mutation and closes on success (kept open on failure for retry); a row's Delete opens the reason-gated
  ContentDialog whose confirm routes to the delete mutation. A successful set/delete re-runs BOTH reads (web invalidates
  the ['system','flags'] query family).
- Data binding (ADR-004): the four manifest data sources are the web hooks useFlags / useFlagChanges / useSetFlag /
  useDeleteFlag. The view-model reads/writes through three injected ports (IFeatureFlagsFeed / IFlagChangesFeed /
  IFlagWriteService, FeatureFlagsPage.Model.cs); the default Empty*/Noop feeds resolve the empty state (the
  DLQInspectorPage/FeedbackQueuePage host-injection precedent), and the generated-client-backed FeatureFlagsClientFeed /
  FlagChangesClientFeed / FlagWriteClientService (FeatureFlagsPage.Source.cs) bind to the generated OpenAPI contract
  client operations get_api_v1_system_flags / get_api_v1_system_flags_changes / put_api_v1_system_flags_key /
  delete_api_v1_system_flags_key, asserted against the generated endpoint table + the FakeApiClient in tests. No HTTP
  touches the view. The PUT body posts the parsed JSON value + reason; the DELETE passes the audit reason as a query
  param. The generated C# client (W1) is regenerated deterministically from api/openapi/teslasync.openapi.json via
  apps/tools/codegen/gen-clients.ts (it is git-ignored, not committed); Generated/Generated.csproj wraps it.
- The web page passes PageContainer only `query={flags}` (not loading/error/empty), so the body always renders the
  children; the flag-registry data states surface per ADR-006 as visible Fluent regions: loading -> the page-tier
  TsDataFreshness chip (IsFetching → "Updating…") + the FlagsTable/ChangesPanel "Loading…" bodies; empty -> the
  FlagsTable "No feature flags are set on this server." empty state + the ChangesPanel "No flag changes yet" empty
  state; success -> the populated registry table + the audit table, FlagsUpdatedAt drives the chip ("Live"). A flags
  read failure drives the freshness chip's IsError ("Error") while the children stay visible (the table falls back to
  its empty branch) — exactly the web behaviour (PageContainer renders no error region of its own). Never a blank region.
- SI units N/A (this admin surface bears no unit fields — flag keys, arbitrary JSON values, actor/operation/reason
  audit rows and timestamps only); the audit timestamps format through the shared DateTimeFormatting port inside the
  composed ChangesPanel at the display boundary.
- All 11 i18n keys already exist verbatim (web key names) in Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw under the
  translation.* prefix (admin.flags.pageTitle/subtitle/actions.add/panels.registry/panels.changes/delete.title/
  delete.message/delete.reasonLabel/delete.reasonPlaceholder/delete.confirm + common.cancel); the surface resolves
  them through the ILocalizer facade with the web English defaults as fallbacks. delete.message is stored with the
  positional {0} marker (the web {{key}} template); DeleteMessage interpolates the flag key.

