# Panels (2) — every web <GlassPanel> reproduced as a Fluent Mica region (TsGlassPanel), each a visible branch
[x] panel  - GlassPanel1   -> registry panel: FeatureFlagsPage.cs#BuildPanel(RegistryGlyph, _registryTitle,
             _flagsTable) — a TsGlassPanel hosting the Flag FontIcon + _registryTitle PanelTitle
             (FeatureFlagsRegistration.PanelRegistry) + the FlagsTable surface bound to
             FeatureFlagsPageViewModel.FlagsModel (web <GlassPanel><Flag/><PanelTitle>Registry</PanelTitle>
             <FlagsTable rows={flags.data?.flags ?? []} loading={flags.isLoading} onEdit onAskDelete/></GlassPanel>);
             edit/delete wired FeatureFlagsPage.cs#OnEditRequested → FlagEditDrawer.ViewModel.Open and
             #OnDeleteRequested → ShowDeleteDialogAsync; test LoadAsync_Success_ReachesReadyState_AndPopulatesBothModels
             (FlagsModel.Rows) + SaveFlagAsync_Success_WritesAndReloads_ReturnsTrue + DeleteFlagAsync_Success_*
[x] panel  - GlassPanel2   -> recent-changes panel: FeatureFlagsPage.cs#BuildPanel(ChangesGlyph, _changesTitle,
             _changesPanel) — a TsGlassPanel hosting the History FontIcon + _changesTitle PanelTitle
             (FeatureFlagsRegistration.PanelChanges) + the ChangesPanel surface bound to
             FeatureFlagsPageViewModel.ChangesModel (global scope, useFlagChanges(null, 50)) (web <GlassPanel>
             <History/><PanelTitle>Recent changes</PanelTitle><ChangesPanel rows={changes.data?.rows ?? []}
             loading={changes.isLoading}/></GlassPanel>); test LoadAsync_Success_ReachesReadyState_AndPopulatesBothModels
             (ChangesModel.Rows single, ChangesModel.Loading false) + ChangesClientFeed_ShapesTheRequest_WithLimit_AndParsesRows

# Data states (3) — loading / empty / success, each a visible region (never blank)
[x] state  - loading       -> FeatureFlagsState.Loading (the VM initial state + while the flags query is in flight):
             FeatureFlagsPage.cs#Render maps it to _freshness.IsFetching (TsDataFreshness "Updating…") and the child
             surfaces' own loading bodies via FlagsModel.Loading / ChangesModel.Loading (FeatureFlagsPageViewModel);
             test InitialState_IsLoading_WithLoadingChildModels
[x] state  - empty         -> the resolved-but-empty branch (FeatureFlagsState.Ready, zero rows): FlagsModel.Rows empty +
             Loading false → the FlagsTable "No feature flags are set on this server." empty state, and ChangesModel.Rows
             empty → the ChangesPanel "No flag changes yet" friendly empty state (FlagsTableState.Empty /
             ChangesPanelState.Empty); test LoadAsync_Empty_ReachesReadyState_WithEmptyModels
[x] state  - success       -> FeatureFlagsState.Ready (both reads resolved with rows): FeatureFlagsPage.cs#Render binds
             the populated FlagsModel/ChangesModel into the registry table + the audit table, FlagsUpdatedAt drives the
             freshness chip ("Live"); a flags read failure instead drives _freshness.IsError ("Error") while the table
             stays visible-empty; tests LoadAsync_Success_ReachesReadyState_AndPopulatesBothModels +
             LoadAsync_FlagsFailure_ReachesErrorState_ButKeepsTheTableVisibleEmpty + LoadAsync_ChangesFailure_KeepsFlagsReady

